<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:34:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Thousands of Colombians march against new right-wing president's policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b4bb8d9022136cfdfffdb389e267bfe66d7702af3d986df37c53f9ab6ece80a</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T01:57:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-thousands-protest-colombia-right-wing-president--3e6c97bc299e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-thousands-protest-colombia-right-wing-president" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Colombians protested peacefully across the country on Wednesday against right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella, in the opposition’s first major demonstrations since he took office in August. Former leftist president Gustavo Petro led a rally in Bogota joined by trade unionists, Indigenous groups, students and feminist activists.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula's party to file complaint against Meta over Brazil election interference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7070d33514fed55d43d8c046903eb99b78bf80a2c2bb7396426a1a5cc08307b4</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:52:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-lula-party-meta-election-interference-brazil-runoff--db9710e4afed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-lula-party-meta-election-interference-brazil-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva’s party plans to file a complaint against Meta with the Organisation of American States alleging election interference, his campaign said Wednesday. The party accuses Meta of restricting Lula’s online content ahead of the October 25 presidential runoff against far-right Senator Flavio Bolsonaro. Meta denies the allegations.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Musk says Zelensky should 'go' as doubts grow over US support for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9d244f5c0a61b77b9c93694a3bfdfcda54eb7c5e64e8161b60f48b44d726ecd</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:34:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:19:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-musk-says-us-govt-responsible-for-any-starshield-restrictions-affecting-ukraine--9dec4e505e36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-musk-says-us-govt-responsible-for-any-starshield-restrictions-affecting-ukraine" /><summary type="html">SpaceX CEO Elon Musk on Wednesday called on Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky to "go" after Kyiv raised doubts over US support for his country against the Russian invasion. A day earlier, Musk said any restrictions on Ukraine's use of the Starshield system would be due to decisions made by the US government after Zelensky called on Musk to restore Starlink, which Kyiv says has been slowed down.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump sparks outrage over AI tiger video after sharing footage of fatal UK attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f002ebea7d466b68044d7054c42fdcd14eeb9af132de4d9c89fa5c4169fe338</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:39:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1--f6bcc553bc17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has sparked outrage after sharing the distressing footage of a 23-year-old man with mental illness being fatally mauled by a tiger at Yorkshire Wildlife Park in the UK, captioned "Don't ever mess with nature!" This was followed hours later by an AI-generated video of himself taming a tiger. The posts have been condemned as disrespectful to the victim and his grieving family, who have urged people to stop sharing harrowing content of the attack. Vedika Bahl tells us more.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>In Phoenix, young ultra-conservatives look to carry on Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4ebb697506c3a97fe8724a88d883fb458cd70edb184b30c4df738736f4fae75</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:37:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy--b1cd212fca53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy" /><summary type="html">More than a year after the assassination of far-right influencer Charlie Kirk in September 2025, young activists from the organisation he co-founded, Turning Point USA, are working tirelessly to honour his legacy by rallying the youth vote ahead of the US midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's crackdown on migrants: New documentary investigates ICE operations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d75d3a7b9bab3f20b93b6a8c6266f148dbdd61f47221e0729dca080d7ec19db</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:51:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261014-trump-s-crackdown-on-migrants-new-documentary-investigates-ice-operations--9b8e9754fee1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261014-trump-s-crackdown-on-migrants-new-documentary-investigates-ice-operations" /><summary type="html">A new documentary from our sister channel France Télévisions explores US President Donald Trump's relentless crackdown on immigration and the agency carrying it out – United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement, better known as ICE. "ICE : La chasse a l'homme", or "A Manhunt Named ICE" interviews agents and also some of the people who lives have been turned upside down by ICE operations. In Perspective, we spoke to the film's co-writer Marine Pradel.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Trump asks US ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign over bribery allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb1fd2e472d25417b1ee416761b1130989e7529e969ad891e068ff9df5094e55</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T03:23:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-trump-asks-us-ambassador-to-greece-kimberly-guilfoyle-to-resign-over-allegations--7d7bb6aaf516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-trump-asks-us-ambassador-to-greece-kimberly-guilfoyle-to-resign-over-allegations" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign on Tuesday after reports alleged she sought $100,000 from a Trump supporter to pay personal credit card debt and accepted luxury trips and hotel stays from wealthy Greek businessmen. Guilfoyle denied wrongdoing and vowed to defend her reputation.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>FBI arrests Saudi OpenAI employee for allegedly bugging San Francisco office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d057919e7ce811b31a603b19da067e7266424008278b94b3bcf0ddaeb5b9e5f</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T23:49:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-fbi-arrests-saudi-openai-employee-for-allegedly-bugging-san-francisco-office--3d35fd945b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-fbi-arrests-saudi-openai-employee-for-allegedly-bugging-san-francisco-office" /><summary type="html">The FBI said on Wednesday it has arrested a Saudi national employed as an engineer at OpenAI on suspicions that he had bugged a conference room at the company's San Francisco office with a "sophisticated recording device".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump asks Greece ambassador to resign amid ethics scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2ba366ea4a7211381dd24a81ba330ccb26b0e0ab0288e204b0082419565de7c</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal--24c18b5f16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-asks-greece-ambassador-to-resign-amid-ethics-scandal" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's administration has asked his ambassador to Greece Kimberly Guilfoyle to resign, the White House said Tuesday, amid allegations that she sought money from a Trump supporter and accepted lavish hospitality from wealthy Greek businessmen. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Former gang leader sentenced to 40 years to life for Tupac Shakur murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47befcfd84972679a50a87c103bf60f7e2fe5479039292ba30df27c00dc5c5e8</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:57:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder--2d6357adbe6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-former-gang-leader-sentenced-to-40-years-to-life-for-tupac-shakur-murder" /><summary type="html">Duane “Keffe D” Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>In Brazil, thousands march fearing return of Bolsonaro presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:037886c05fe57e4bbdaa4ae7af37887f4c30a0a589e57901232b4c71771201aa</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T14:59:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency--752369db782e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-brazil-thousands-march-fearing-return-of-bolsonaro-presidency" /><summary type="html">Thousands of young Brazilians have taken to the streets to support President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and voice fears of a return to power for the Bolsonaro political movement, amid a closely watched presidential race. Many protesters say they are worried about their future, particularly the impact a far-right government could have on universities and education. FRANCE 24’s Jan Onoszko reports from Brazil.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump’s use of Russian diesel fuel, at Ukraine’s expense, sparks controversy in the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24f33430c8bf171bc474e6a3aef404756aa5c71fe3e2c242a5b2eb0a12201c4d</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T13:26:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-s-use-of-russian-diesel-fuel-at-ukraine-s-expense-sparks-controversy-in-the-us--8dd3eba1a3a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-s-use-of-russian-diesel-fuel-at-ukraine-s-expense-sparks-controversy-in-the-us" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump’s plan to import Russian diesel despite Western sanctions has sparked fierce criticism in Washington, including from Republicans, as high fuel prices and the upcoming midterm elections put pressure on his administration. His approach to the Ukraine war has also drawn controversy, with calls for Kyiv to hold elections and claims of an energy ceasefire announced without clear agreement from the parties involved. FRANCE 24's Douglas Herbert has the analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>US economists win Nobel for research helping policymakers navigate crises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:679f29590c8f7d09153d6c29e521ea8ca044d7c492eb3b1bbe7f902931d56911</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T10:04:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-economists-win-nobel-for-research-helping-policymakers-navigate-crises--ba65e32638f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-economists-win-nobel-for-research-helping-policymakers-navigate-crises" /><summary type="html">Two American economists, Robert E. Hall of Stanford University and Michael Woodford of Columbia University, have won the Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences for their work on economic stabilisation. Their research helps policymakers and central banks better understand economic fluctuations, manage recessions and inflation, and account for public expectations when shaping economic policy. The prize money, worth around $1.2 million, will be shared equally between the two laureates.</summary></entry><entry><title>US immigration authorities raid home of Democratic Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b5baccd046b2c41b819b3b031383d4318e61b3cb151e4df782a9d4300a3d620</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-immigration-authorities-raid-home-of-democratic-trump-critic-ilhan-omar--1003e5999102.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-immigration-authorities-raid-home-of-democratic-trump-critic-ilhan-omar" /><summary type="html">US authorities raided the Washington home of Democratic Representative Ilhan Omar on Monday as part of an ongoing investigation into alleged immigration fraud, according to reports. The probe reportedly includes immigration paperwork completed by her late father when she was a child. Omar accused the Trump administration of using government institutions to target political opponents, describing the raid as an act of political intimidation. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson has the latest from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Breaking Bad' actor and disability activist RJ Mitte dies aged 34</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff551c27f14ff7b7d350019ff6697c11774747581ae4e3e51596dfe960083d40</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T01:43:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-activist-rj-mitte-dies-aged-34--e0f5ef5dfa82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261013-breaking-bad-actor-and-disability-activist-rj-mitte-dies-aged-34" /><summary type="html">"Breaking Bad" actor RJ Mitte, who played Walter White Jr. in the hit US television series, has died aged 34, his representatives said Monday. The actor, who lived with cerebal palsy, also became a prominent disability rights advocate, championing inclusion and representation in film and television.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US federal agents raid home of Democratic congresswoman and Trump critic Ilhan Omar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e39c8d8f4b2fcdc13b2b73a79d941009b08ff6da3b3753e33cdae3e32987a283</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:13:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar--1078c3e6f713.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-us-federal-agents-raid-home-of-democratic-congresswoman-and-trump-critic-ilhan-omar" /><summary type="html">US federal agents on Monday launched a raid on ‌the Washington home of Democratic representative Ilhan Omar, an outspoken critic of US President Donald ⁠Trump, officials said. The raid followed a criminal fraud ‌investigation into the Somali-born lawmaker's immigration paperwork submitted by her late father when she ⁠was a child, Fox News reported.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Capital punishment in US: Elected judges, prosecutors seek 'results', 'not interested in the truth'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d7661bfa573c9e4744816b6ffdf38453ca4c628d506cbea2ffb5a56db865722</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T13:27:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-trut--c9271d966485.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261012-capital-punishment-in-us-elected-judges-prosecutors-seek-results-not-interested-in-the-truth" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Sandrine Ageorges-Skinner, an advocate against the death penalty, author and member of the association "Ensemble contre la peine de mort" (Together Against the Death Penalty). She asserts that capital punishment is "really a political agenda, especially in electoral times."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Inside Jeffrey Epstein's network: How favours, money and influence kept it running</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5208501bd4a91300448358ed14988d96523f261bc30a7025bbbd9bab97a60592</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T11:36:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-inside-jeffrey-epstein-s-network-how-favours-money-and-influence-kept-it-running--a47863837826.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261012-inside-jeffrey-epstein-s-network-how-favours-money-and-influence-kept-it-running" /><summary type="html">For years, convicted sexual predator Jeffrey Epstein developed a global web of powerful connections despite accusations of sex trafficking. Millions of declassified documents reveal how he expanded and maintainted his network.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula accuses social media giant Meta of election interference amid tight run-off campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3ab7d49a21b007b1c6018ade3f21fd87d58e52d9b049523443374df6bd44f84</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T13:12:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-brazil-lula-accuses-social-media-giant-meta-election-interference-amid-tight-run-campaign--d8ebedff7d11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-brazil-lula-accuses-social-media-giant-meta-election-interference-amid-tight-run-campaign" /><summary type="html">Social media platform Meta has 48 hours to respond to claims by Brazil's leftwing candidate and incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's campaign accusing the tech platform of blocking content on the company's platforms. Brazil's Superior Electoral Court on Saturday gave the social media giant 48 hours to clarify whether it reduced the reach of posts by Lula's campaign ahead of the tight October 25 run-off against rightwing candidate Flavio Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Convicted murderer Christa Pike leaves hospital, returns to prison after botched execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0150032778a5757b2781e3c7f2af9d75e460519db77a383250624916a364055e</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T17:41:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-leaves-hospital-returns-to-prison-after-botched-execution--557dbe1b2584.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-leaves-hospital-returns-to-prison-after-botched-execution" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike's lawyers on Saturday said that the 50-year-old convicted murderer has been discharged from the hospital and returned to prison. Pike was transported to the hospital in critical condition on September 30 after she survived Tennessee's botched effort to execute her for murdering a classmate when she was a teenager.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US, Europe and Ukraine hold 'constructive discussions' on joint plan to end war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc59808581ce072d3776886254b3d6035f3f55308767e9790c96908dc9ca7625</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T07:47:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-us-ukrainians-europeans-discuss-new-ideas-to-end-war-diesel--5af96e215021.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-us-ukrainians-europeans-discuss-new-ideas-to-end-war-diesel" /><summary type="html">US, Ukrainian and European negotiators held talks in Miami on Friday to seek a common proposal to end the war in Ukraine, as President Donald Trump's decision to ease restrictions on Russian fuel drew criticism from lawmakers and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Powerful 7.6 magnitude quake shakes Panama, triggering tsunami warnings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5edb69cdd8ab2666645955dd9b0fd89b0d46951877a1c7c2410e5decdcd6fce</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T18:39:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning--2b8cfe163ef0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning" /><summary type="html">A strong 7.6 magnitude earthquake struck near the southern ​coast ‌of Panama ⁠on Friday at a 10 km depth, ‌according to the US Geological ⁠Survey, shaking buildings as far away as the capital and prompting evacuations. The US Tsunami Warning ​System showed potential tsunami threats across much of Central America's Pacific ​coast.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Unweaving Jeffrey Epstein’s web: What the files have revealed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbb0cb038ac0e46cf4221aeeb0872d5b70daa3f00d560f2f0081219fee1d46ac</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T17:00:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-unweaving-jeffrey-epstein-s-web-what-the-files-have-revealed--84e88b833ace.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-unweaving-jeffrey-epstein-s-web-what-the-files-have-revealed" /><summary type="html">On January 30, 2026, the US Justice Department released 3 million documents. Photos, videos, emails, text messages, court records... All connected to one man: Jeffrey Epstein. Since then, media outlets around the world have brought to light the vast amount of people that appear in the Epstein files. Eight months on, what what do these revelations tell us about Jeffrey Epstein’s network? How did it operate? FRANCE 24 journalist Ava Luquet spent months digging through the files. In this video, she takes a closer look at what they reveal about the predator’s network and its inner workings.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pentagon vows to livestream first military execution in decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3380d485d89681f2851bc8c976e23b8e5f2cd163ff19257be41beb65460291e6</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T10:56:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-pentagon-vows-to-livestream-first-military-execution-in-decades--b2bdc97d8c93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-pentagon-vows-to-livestream-first-military-execution-in-decades" /><summary type="html">The first US military execution in more than 65 years will be livestreamed, announced the Pentagon on Thursday, after Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said it would be "public".
 
Former Army psychiatrist Nidal Hasan opened fire at Fort Hood in Texas in 2009, killing 13 people. His execution will take place at the military base on December 3, 2026.
 
 "The livestreaming of an execution is tantamount to a public execution and would breach the absolute prohibition of torture," the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights said on Friday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hegseth says Fort Hood shooter's military execution will be 'livestreamed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f681a9370d3e88e7df7b626b3a409947dede95bead47bbec2d5809007a03140</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T09:39:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261009-hegseth-says-fort-hood-shooter-s-military-execution-will-be-livestreamed--5b4541a054d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261009-hegseth-says-fort-hood-shooter-s-military-execution-will-be-livestreamed" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 9: US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth announces that the military execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Malik Hasan will be "livestreamed". But first: we look at reactions in Italy after the country's parliament passes a controversial electoral reform that critics say serves to benefit Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni. Plus, ".fart" and ".trump" are among the new domain name applications, as revealed by the US non-profit organisation ICANN.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>New York mayor to ask Trump for ICE withdrawal after agents shoot man in car with child</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88b410a4b8ab0718ecc6dc5d3c95b91f9004891682d37aa5df952ae5337e1033</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T05:21:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-new-york-mayor-calls-for-ice-removal-after-man-shot-with-5-year-old-nearby--d5f97c1e038b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-new-york-mayor-calls-for-ice-removal-after-man-shot-with-5-year-old-nearby" /><summary type="html">New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani has said he will ask US President Donald Trump to remove ICE from the city after federal immigration agents on Thursday shot a man in a vehicle with his five-year-old child during an attempted arrest. The 28-year-old survived and is being treated at hospital.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro wins support of third-place candidate in presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aaf6a43c2aea1fe1c4b5ca1a44d7a290c3726feb87df9ac3948e9e48f978916</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T02:34:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-third-place-candidate-lula--1725ac1116b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-third-place-candidate-lula" /><summary type="html">Brazil's right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro secured third-place finisher Augusto Cury's endorsement on Thursday, strengthening his position against incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva ahead of the runoff. Cury won nearly three percent in Sunday's first round. A Datafolha poll put Bolsonaro ahead with 52 percent against Lula's 48 percent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Families reunited as USS Lincoln returns from troubled 10-month deployment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc199076cd0ab47f5570b298f3b8a459d30b70365b29bd01beda4cea2661cba1</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T00:13:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-families-reunited-as-uss-lincoln-comes-home-after-troubled-gulf-deployment--a048e64efea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-families-reunited-as-uss-lincoln-comes-home-after-troubled-gulf-deployment" /><summary type="html">The USS Lincoln docked in California on Thursday ending a record deployment of 265 days of uninterrupted time at sea marked by reports of deteriorating conditions onboard. Crew members were reunited with family they had not seen in nearly a year after their mission was prolonged by the war in Iran.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US files new torture charges against  Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro and wife Cilia Flores</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcf730e186a437efdde3c8afad80856c86881036240811df471cf10cda6cb6a5</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T23:56:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-us-files-new-torture-charges-venezuela-nicolas-maduro-cilia-flores--cb767909dc08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-us-files-new-torture-charges-venezuela-nicolas-maduro-cilia-flores" /><summary type="html">The United States on Thursday charged ousted Venezuelan president Nicolas Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores with conspiracy to commit torture, adding to drug trafficking and firearms charges. Prosecutors allege detainees, including US citizens, suffered waterboarding, rape and beatings. The pair remain in US custody following a January military raid.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Fort Hood shooter’s firing squad execution to be livestreamed, Pentagon says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:118a2bb3e6793f04f511b7b2c5a3bc322b504870313eca82bd4cbb4d3ad898ab</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T22:01:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-fort-hood-shooter-firing-squad-execution-livestreamed-pentagon--59347f674512.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-fort-hood-shooter-firing-squad-execution-livestreamed-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The Pentagon said on Thursday the firing squad execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Malik Hasan would be livestreamed on December 3 after Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth vowed to make the execution "public". Hasan was convicted of killing 13 people and injuring 32 in a 2009 shooting at the Texas military base. The UN on Friday condemned the decision as "torture".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
